What's to "fix"?

NetHack is best played as a puzzle. The whole
concept that the game has to be rewritten (read:
"gutted") every single time someone finds (and
publishes) a canned solution for that puzzle, or
starts churning out packaged "Solution Helper" is
just a denial of reality. If the puzzle can be
solved, the solution can be canned or helpers for it
packaged. If the puzzle cannot be solved, the game
is unplayable.

"Spoilers" are just another attempt to package
solution helpers at the detail level.

> ((However, I'm still not convinced that the devs
> should change the code.))

Indeed not. No one is *forced* to use scripts, to
pudding farm, to farm Kops, to farm quest monsters,
to read spoilers, to patch the game to automate
winning by making it a munchkin paradise. These are
all _personal choices_.

More importantly, probably, the DevTeam should be
left to the business of _enhancing_ the game, not
placed in the adversarial role of continually
countering the community's cleverness by being
